From ea0ac3f56be8ef0329344db3e9bdb52154f44093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 11:41:10 -1000
Subject: [PATCH 40/63] [cuttlefish] Add --enable_qemu_display flag for
 headless macOS operation

Summary:
# Motivation:

On macOS, QEMU opens a Cocoa display window for each emulator instance. The hypothesis is it's crashing in RE because it's trying to reserve a window.

# Overview:

- add --enable_qemu_display flag (default: true) to launch_cvd/assemble_cvd. This is non-breaking since it's additive. It only causes and issue if used with an old set of host tools. Upstream is not compatible with macOS anyways, so no risk there.

Test Plan:
```
cd /Volumes/AOSP && source build/envsetup.sh && lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug && m assemble_cvd run_cvd
./start_cuttlefish.py --enable_qemu_display=false
```
no window just adb
 {F1986710810}

